'\" t
.TH "ACTON\-DISASM" "1"
.nh
.ad l
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "NAME"
acton\-disasm \[em] Disassemble TVM bytecode into human\-readable TASM
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBacton disasm\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIboc\-file\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Disassemble compiled TVM bytecode from a file, a literal BoC string, or a live
contract address.
.sp
This command is useful for debugging compiler output, inspecting deployed code,
following library references, and correlating bytecode with Tolk source via
source maps.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.SS "Disassembly Options"
.sp
\fIboc\-file\fR
.RS 4
Binary, hex, or base64 BoC file to disassemble.
.sp
Use \fB\-\-string\fR to pass the code directly instead of reading a file.
.sp
Available since trunk.
.sp
A \fB\&.tolk\fR file is compiled as an entrypoint before disassembly. Imports use the
project mappings from \fBActon.toml\fR\&. Files without an entrypoint are also accepted.
Use \fB\-\-function\fR to select individual functions from these sources.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-function\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Available since trunk.
.sp
Disassemble only the named function from a \fB\&.tolk\fR input. Repeat this option to
select multiple functions, including functions declared in imported files.
Functions are printed in the requested order; repeated names are printed once.
All names in one invocation share the same compilation passes.
.sp
Selected functions keep separate bytecode bodies, even if normally inlined or
unused. This inspection build leaves source files and build artifacts
unchanged. Its bytecode can differ from a normal optimized build.
.sp
Supports non\-generic functions with block bodies and no receiver or \fBmutate\fR
parameters, get\-methods, and external entrypoints. Get\-methods and functions with
an explicit \fB@method_id\fR keep their IDs. Generic functions, receiver methods,
\fBasm\fR functions, and \fBonBouncedMessage\fR cannot be selected.
.sp
Requires a \fB\&.tolk\fR file. Cannot be used with \fB\-\-source\-map\fR, \fB\-\-string\fR,
\fB\-\-address\fR, or \fB\-\-follow\-libraries\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-string\fR \fIstring\fR
.RS 4
BoC value in hex or base64 format.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Write plain disassembly text to a file.
.sp
Without \fB\-\-json\fR, this replaces standard output. With \fB\-\-json\fR, Acton still
prints the JSON envelope to stdout and writes only the \fBassembly\fR field to the
file.
.sp
If the parent directory does not exist, Acton creates it automatically.
Existing files are overwritten.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-show\-hashes\fR
.RS 4
Show cell hashes alongside code blocks.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-show\-offsets\fR
.RS 4
Show instruction bit offsets in the left column.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS 4
Print machine\-readable disassembly JSON to stdout.
.sp
Successful output includes \fBsuccess\fR, the plain disassembly in \fBassembly\fR, and
\fBblocks\fR derived from \fB\-\-source\-map\fR or the compiled Tolk source.
For BoC input without \fB\-\-source\-map\fR, \fBblocks\fR is empty.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-source\-map\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Use a source map to show original Tolk source locations together with
disassembly output.
.sp
Available since trunk.
.sp
This option applies to BoC input. Recompiled \fB\&.tolk\fR input does not accept an
external source map.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-address\fR \fIaddress\fR
.RS 4
Fetch contract code from the blockchain by address and disassemble it.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-net\fR \fInetwork\fR
.RS 4
Network to use for \fB\-\-address\fR and library lookups.
.sp
Supported values: \fBmainnet\fR, \fBtestnet\fR, \fBlocalnet\fR, \fBcustom:<name>\fR\&.
.sp
\fBlocalnet\fR and \fBcustom:<name>\fR resolve through the project network
configuration in \fBActon.toml\fR\&.
.sp
If omitted, Acton tries mainnet first and then falls back to testnet.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-follow\-libraries\fR
.RS 4
If the input disassembles to exactly one top\-level exotic library\-reference
cell, fetch and disassemble the actual library code instead of showing only the
library hash reference.
.sp
This is not a general recursive library\-follow mode.
.RE
.SS "Display Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIwhen\fR
.RS 4
Control when to use colored output.
.sp
Possible values: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR
.RE
.SS "Project Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the \fBActon.toml\fR file to use for this invocation.
.sp
Use this when running the command outside the project directory or when the
manifest lives at a non\-default location.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-project\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the project root to use for configuration discovery and relative
defaults.
.sp
This conflicts with \fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR\&.
.RE
.SH "BLOCKCHAIN LOOKUPS"
When \fB\-\-address\fR is used, Acton fetches code from the selected network.
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-net\fR accepts \fBmainnet\fR, \fBtestnet\fR, \fBlocalnet\fR, and \fBcustom:<name>\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBlocalnet\fR and \fBcustom:<name>\fR use URLs from \fBActon.toml\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'Without \fB\-\-net\fR, Acton tries mainnet first and then testnet
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'with \fB\-\-address\fR, \fB\-\-follow\-libraries\fR reuses the network that returned the
contract code
.RE
.sp
When \fB\-\-follow\-libraries\fR is used with a local file or \fB\-\-string\fR, Acton uses
the explicit \fB\-\-net\fR if provided; otherwise library fetches default to
testnet.
.SH "TON CENTER API KEYS"
Built\-in \fBmainnet\fR/\fBtestnet\fR requests read \fBTONCENTER_MAINNET_API_KEY\fR or
\fBTONCENTER_TESTNET_API_KEY\fR, depending on the selected network.
.sp
For \fBcustom:<name>\fR, Acton reads \fB<NORMALIZED_NAME>_API_KEY\fR\&. Custom network
names are uppercased and non\-alphanumeric characters are replaced with \fB_\fR, so
\fBcustom:mock\-remote\fR becomes \fBMOCK_REMOTE_API_KEY\fR\&.
.sp
Acton loads \fB\&.env\fR automatically, so the simplest setup during project work is
usually to keep these keys there and use shell environment variables only for
one\-off overrides or CI.
.SH "INPUT PRECEDENCE"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBBOC_FILE\fR and \fB\-\-string\fR are mutually exclusive
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-address\fR is used only when neither a file nor \fB\-\-string\fR is provided
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-follow\-libraries\fR only replaces the input when the initial disassembly is
exactly one top\-level exotic library\-reference cell and the lookup succeeds
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'ordinary code, mixed instruction streams, or nested library references are a
no\-op for \fB\-\-follow\-libraries\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'if library lookup fails, Acton warns and disassembles the original code
instead; this still exits successfully
.RE
.SH "SOURCE MAPS"
If you compiled a contract with \fBacton compile \-\-source\-map\fR, you can pass that
source map JSON here to annotate the disassembly with original Tolk locations.
.sp
\fB\-\-source\-map\fR only affects annotations in the output. It does not change which
BoC is disassembled.
.SH "JSON OUTPUT"
With \fB\-\-json\fR, Acton prints pretty\-printed JSON to stdout.
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBsuccess\fR: \fBtrue\fR for successful disassembly
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBassembly\fR: plain disassembly text without inline source\-map comments
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBblocks\fR: source\-to\-assembly mappings derived from \fB\-\-source\-map\fR
.RE
.sp
Each item in \fBblocks\fR contains a \fBsource\fR location and \fBassembly_ranges\fR\&.
\fBassembly_ranges\fR stores inclusive zero\-based \fBstart_line\fR/\fBend_line\fR pairs
into the \fBassembly\fR string.
.sp
For BoC input, \fBblocks\fR is empty without \fB\-\-source\-map\fR\&.
Tolk source input includes mappings from its inspection compilation automatically.
.sp
If \fB\-\-output\fR is also provided, the output file contains the same plain
\fBassembly\fR text while stdout remains JSON.
.sp
Available since trunk.
.sp
With \fB\-\-function\fR, the response also includes a \fBfunctions\fR array in the requested
order. Each item contains \fBname\fR, \fBmethod_id\fR, \fBassembly\fR, \fBblocks\fR, and \fBgas_estimate\fR\&.
The per\-function \fBassembly\fR contains only that function\[cq]s instructions.
Its \fBblocks\fR use line offsets into that function\[cq]s \fBassembly\fR; top\-level \fBblocks\fR
use offsets into the combined \fBassembly\fR, including function headers.
Source locations refer to the original files, before annotation overrides.
Identical bytecode may share a cell whose source marks were retained for only one
function. Functions without matching marks have empty \fBblocks\fR; Acton does not
attribute another function\[cq]s source locations to them.
.sp
\fBgas_estimate\fR contains:
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBvalue\fR: sum of the lowest listed opcode costs from the bundled TVM specification
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBhas_dynamic_cost\fR: costs depend on runtime data or include a formula
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBhas_control_flow\fR: the body contains control flow or nested continuations
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBunknown_instructions\fR: instructions whose cost could not be included
.RE
.sp
The estimate counts each instruction and nested continuation once. It does not
predict the path taken through branches or the number of loop iterations.
It excludes callees, implicit returns, dispatcher overhead, stack\-copy charges,
and additional data\-dependent fees. It is neither a lower nor an upper bound on
runtime gas. Use execution profiling when inputs and actual gas costs matter.
.sp
For example, \fBfun increment(value: int): int { return value + 1; }\fR has this entry:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
{
  "name": "increment",
  "method_id": 262143,
  "assembly": "INC\(rsn",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "source": {"file": "example.tolk", "line": 1, "column": 41, "end_line": 1, "end_column": 50},
      "assembly_ranges": [{"start_line": 0, "end_line": 0}]
    }
  ],
  "gas_estimate": {
    "value": 18,
    "has_dynamic_cost": false,
    "has_control_flow": false,
    "unknown_instructions": 0
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.sp
Generated method IDs are local to the inspection build. Identify functions by
\fBname\fR when matching results to an editor document.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB0\fR: Disassembly completed successfully, including runs with unresolved
library references that were left as warnings.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB1\fR: BoC input was invalid, a blockchain fetch failed, source\-map loading
failed, or the output file could not be written.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Available since trunk.
.sp
Disassemble selected functions from a Tolk entrypoint:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm contracts/jetton\-wallet.tolk \-\-function transfer \-\-function get_wallet_data
.fi
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'Disassemble a local BoC file:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm contract.boc
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'Disassemble a literal BoC string:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm \-\-string "b5ee9c72010104...0840f01c700f2f4"
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'Disassemble code from a blockchain address:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm \-\-address UQA_ftKIJsHEAE_UgtFOUK15hPzycZooFuUr8duyY9T3kwwM \-\-net testnet
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'Show hashes, offsets, and source locations:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm contract.boc \-\-show\-hashes \-\-show\-offsets \-\-source\-map contract.json
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'Inspect deployed code together with hashes:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm \-\-address UQA_ftKIJsHEAE_UgtFOUK15hPzycZooFuUr8duyY9T3kwwM \-\-show\-hashes \(rs
                                                                        \-\-net testnet
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 6.\h'+01'Write disassembly to a nested output path:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm contract.boc \-\-output build/disasm/contract.tasm
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 7.\h'+01'Resolve a top\-level library\-reference cell using a configured custom network:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm library\-ref.boc \-\-follow\-libraries \-\-net custom:staging
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 8.\h'+01'Print machine\-readable JSON with source\-map ranges:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton disasm contract.boc \-\-source\-map contract.json \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBacton help compile\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fIDisassembly command guide\fR <https://ton\-blockchain.github.io/acton/docs/commands/disasm>
.RE
